SUMMARY:Naturalist Ed Series: Observing and Identifying Plants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T130000
UID:260820E2jwLKtY4kutBFUdVEGMEA
DESCRIPTION:Native plants provide shelter and food for wildlife and suppor
 t pollinators. Join us to learn about plant diversity at the Osborn Preser
 ve! We will explore a variety of vegetation communities including oak wood
 land\, riparian\, grassland and more where we will observe plants through 
 sight\, touch and smell. Find out what different types of plants are up to
  this late summer season.
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/observing_and_identifying_plants
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
