DESCRIPTION:With a bag of cookies and a good spot in the yard to read his 
 comic book\, Boy was ready for a perfectly peaceful day. But then... Mouse
  came. He may be adorable\, but he's full of questions. And energy. And he
 's hungry. What can Boy do but give Mouse a cookie? Wouldn't you do the sa
 me thing? But if you give a mouse a cookie\, he's going to want a glass of
  milk...\n\nJody Davidson's adaptation\, based on the books by Laura Joffe
  Numeroff\, is a mayhem- and mishap-filled joyride for all audiences.\n\n*
 *Show details**\n\nAuthors: Adapted by Jody Davidson\, based on the books 
 by Laura Joffe Numeroff\n\nLocation: Cinnabar Theater Studio Space\, 2200 
 Petaluma Blvd N.\, Suite 700\, Petaluma\n\nPerformance dates: Sat Aug 22 (
 11am & 2pm)\, Sun Aug 23 (11am)\, Sat Aug 29 (11am & 2pm)\, Sun Aug 30 (11
 am)\n\nEstimated run time: 60 minutes\n\nRecommended for ages 3+. Children
  under 3 are welcome to attend at the discretion of their parent or caregi
 ver. You know your child best! If your little one is ready for a live thea
 ter experience\, we’d love to have them join the adventure.\n\nTickets: 
 https://cinnabartheater.org/show/mouseacookie/
LOCATION:Cinnabar Studio Space at the Petaluma Village Premium Outlets #70
 0
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/mouseacookie/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
