DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, August 22\, 2026 1:00. PM- 4:00 PM\n\nL
 ocation\n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n
 \nEvent Category: Fiber Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n13\\+\n\nChildren under the 
 age of 18 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n$93 – Registration Cost $7
  – Materials Fee $100 – Total Registration Cost\n\nJoin us for a playf
 ul dive into an ancient craft. The peyote stitch has been used for thousan
 ds of years across many cultures. In this fun class you’ll create a bold
  beautiful ring using the Even Count Flat Peyote stitch. We’ll cover eve
 rything you need to confidently start your own bead weaving journey.All ma
 terials \\(thread\, needles\, beads\\) will be provided for the workshop. 
 If students would like to buy needles and thread to take home they can pur
 chase them directly from the instructor after the workshop for a minimal f
 ee. Resources for beading supplies will also be provided.Finger dexterity 
 and good close-up vision are needed for this workshop. Bring your best rea
 ding glasses!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/beaded-ring-workshop/
