BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Harvest Table at Somerston Estate – August
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T140000
UID:260803rBsLafb1bkaLGYphFtUZ8w
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable afternoon at Somerston Estate as 
 we celebrate the start of harvest season with an elevated wine and culinar
 y experience. Surrounded by rolling vineyards and stunning mountain vistas
 \, guests will enjoy a chef-curated multi-course lunch from Chef Cameron B
 ouldin\, thoughtfully paired with estate-grown wines from Somerston Estate
  and Priest Ranch.\n\nAs the vineyards begin their annual transformation f
 rom growing season to harvest\, guests will experience the anticipation an
 d excitement that fills the estate during this special time of year. Follo
 wing lunch\, you’ll enjoy a tour of our production area\, where you’ll
  learn about the harvest process\, see how the winery prepares for its bus
 iest season\, and sample wine straight from the barrel. While harvest may 
 just be getting underway\, you’ll gain a unique glimpse into the work th
 at happens behind the scenes as a new vintage begins its journey.\n\nWith 
 the warm summer we’ve been experiencing\, there’s even a chance we’l
 l catch the first signs of harvest in action!\n\nExceptional wines\, remar
 kable food\, breathtaking views\, and an exclusive look behind the cellar 
 doors await. We look forward to welcoming you to the table at Somerston Es
 tate.\n\nReserve your seat and toast the start of harvest with us!
LOCATION:Somerston Estate Winery & Vineyard
URL:https://priestranchwines.com/visit/?gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=236353
 96516&gbraid=0AAAAACRIXxxwQ4s4zPHvKy3jkr6XxoP2y&gclid=Cj0KCQjwo_PRBhDNARIs
 AEcVALVjGF-VEByrWM1KJ4j32Rxmiy4SKYvV4wItvJ8iCqGPA0uzETZN6dsaAptLEALw_wcB#
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visiting Artist Demo with Todd Barricklow: Slab Vessels and Sgraff
 ito Demo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T163000
UID:260803kzsQClyL9U2lU_J-dxCqBQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 22\, 2026\n\n12:00 PM – 4:30 PM\n\nLocatio
 n\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Workshops\n\nExp
 erience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\
 n\n$65\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$65\n\
 nJoin us for a dynamic\, professional four-hour workshop that bridges the 
 worlds of structural form and intricate surface design. Drawing from a ric
 h background in printmaking and design\, your instructor will guide you th
 rough his process of creating substantial ceramic works with compelling vi
 sual narratives.\n\nSegment 1: Large-Scale Slab Building Demo \\(2 Hours\\
 ): Discover the architecture of clay as we spend the first half of the cla
 ss focusing on the construction of a large vessel. Todd will demonstrate h
 ow to roll out slabs\, manage drying times\, and assemble pieces that main
 tain their integrity through the firing process.\n\nSegment 2: Sgraffito S
 urface Design \\(2 Hours\\): Explore the history and modern application of
  Sgraffito. This segment covers essential tools\, composition strategies\,
  and carving methods. You will learn the importance of the “sweet spot
 ”—the perfect moisture level for carving—to ensure clean designs.\n\
 nTo fully immerse you in the technique\, every participant will be provide
 d with a pre-prepared greenware tile coated in black slip. This will allow
  you to practice carving techniques that can serve as a texture reference 
 on your clay. Dive in to the structural possibilities of clay and the grap
 hic potential of its surface! Please note: Your tiles are for practice and
  will not be fired after the class.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/slab-vessels-and-sgraffito-
 demo/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T170000
UID:260803gPNxaVR6k0iX37mH5ADd4g
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leap of Legend: An Immersive Sensory Experience at Stags' Leap Win
 ery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
UID:26080304jvukUykk-ZuKp33ldy_g
DESCRIPTION:Step beyond the traditional tasting and into the legend of Sta
 gs’ Leap. Created in partnership with ThemeDream Productions\, Leap o
 f Legend is a limited-run immersive experience that brings the winery’s
  storied past to life through theatrical environments\, narration\, lighti
 ng\, sound\, interactive elements\, and wine. \n\n Guided through a seri
 es of richly imagined rooms inside the historic Manor House\, guests will 
 move from the legend of the stag to the intrigue of Prohibition and beyond
 . Along the way\, hidden details\, sensory moments\, and a few unexpected 
 discoveries invite you deeper into the story.
LOCATION:Stags' Leap Winery
URL:https://www.stagsleap.com/pages/leap-of-legend
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
