SUMMARY:24/7 Theatre Without a Safety Net!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T193000
UID:260716NalRJiGA_0aVyIIb6af1jg
DESCRIPTION:**The details:** Seven writers\, seven directors\, and seven 
 groups of actors gather together Friday\, August 21st\, at the Raven and\,
  with the help of the audience\, select a theme that will inspire the writ
 ers to each write a ten-minute play. **The audience also votes on one line
  of dialogue that must be in each play.** The writers then have until 8 a
 m Saturday to write their plays\; the directors and actors rehearse from 1
 0 am to 4 pm\, returning to the Raven at 4:30 to do a quick tech run in pr
 eparation for performing all seven plays at 7:30 pm to an eager and enthus
 iastic audience.\n\nJoin us for theatre like you’ve never experienced be
 fore — your ticket is good for both nights!\n\n**ATTENTION ACTORS AND DI
 RECTORS:** How do you join the madcap fun? Simple: Email Steven David Mar
 tin at steven.d.m@raventheater.org if you would like to act\, write\, or 
 direct. The more\, the merrier!\n\n**August 21st\, 7:30pm:** Audience sel
 ects a theme to guide the playwrights.\n\n**Aug 22nd\, 7:30pm:** Performan
 ce of all seven 10-minute plays created in the previous 24 hours!\n\n**7:3
 0 PM** **nightly**\n\n**Admission:** $25 (ticket includes both nights).
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/24-7-theatre-without-a-safety-net/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T180000
UID:260715kf4geZ1hjkSVU9y4XukpMg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T180000
UID:260715jXKI8EHsdkqSO6LbCUJC_w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\n**AUGUST EXHIBIT: PAI
 NTING IN FAUVE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  **July 27 – August 30\, 2026**\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow La
 Land and Gen Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be
  sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautif
 ul work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma wi
 ne country artist\, **Willow LaLand** presents **Painting in Fauve\,** a c
 ollection of oil and acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant 
 beauty through the artist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realisti
 c landscapes\, these works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, t
 apping into the wild Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\
 , “Mt. Tamalpais” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over 
 its undulating slopes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mo
 untain’s grandeur.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with c
 olor as it overlooks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us fro
 m palette to palate as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine re
 d wine in “Sommelier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\
 , LaLand notes “I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in co
 lor\, and give a tangible realistic impression within a completely fantast
 ical expression.”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her stud
 ies as a young girl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspi
 red by early American realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve 
 dramatic realism.  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful 
 response to her themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love b
 oth her styles and have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing
  between the two.  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, a
 nd participated in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American 
 Art Collector magazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: La
 Land will host the Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\,
  11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Gen Zorich
 ’s Summertime\,** highlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth
  of long\, lazy summer days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist a
 nd environmental scientist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understa
 nding of the natural world. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating 
 on pastel pads in “Summer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy d
 ays.  These works would bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of
  year.  An award-winning artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has bee
 n a longtime participant in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Zorich will host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, A
 ugust 4\, 11am to 6 pm and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE
  Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event 
 celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating. This 
 month’s special theme: Music and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 43
 1-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wilderness First Aid Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T170000
UID:260711t-ER-qbX8Uq574zbQrSr3w
DESCRIPTION:First aid training lead by Safety Training Pros\, classes
  are fun with lots of hands-on skills practice. The emphasis is
  on making good decisions by staying calm and safe\, doing a g
 ood patient assessment\, and having good communication and leaders
 hip. \n\nJoin our classes\, where it is safe to learn and OK t
 o make mistakes. Wilderness First Aid is 16 hours \\(two 8-hour
  days\\) and focuses on practicing skills and covering patient a
 ssessment\, shock and bleeding\, head and spinal injuries\, wounds
 \, musculoskeletal injuries\, and heat and cold illnesses. It als
 o includes a half-day of outdoor scenario practice of first aid
  and leadership skills. \n\nGain the tools and knowledge to hand
 le a wilderness first aid emergency. Registration includes day us
 e fee and class materials. Successful completion of the class in
 cludes a Wilderness First Aid certificate.\n\nThe instructor will 
 additionally offer a one-hour CPR/AED course immediately after the
  Wilderness First Aid course. The course will focus on both adu
 lts and children and comes with a 2-year certification.\n\nCamping
  will be available at the group camp for those who wish to ca
 mp on Saturday and Sunday night at no additional cost. Camping 
 might also be available Friday night in the general campground a
 rea on a first-come\, first-serve basis for an additional $20 pe
 r participant.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/summerwfa2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Beginner Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T130000
UID:260701OevY-Qj43k-GN5IMIGL-JQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe following is a list of possible routes selected fo
 r this hiking series: 1\\) Sat 8/1 - White Barn to Uranus\, 2.1
  miles\, 180 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 2\\) Sat 8/8 - Me
 adow- Hillside loop\, 3 miles\, 490 ft elev \\[meet @ white bar
 n\\] 3\\) Sat 8/15 - Lake Ralphine & Spring Lake loop\, 4.3 mil
 es\, 420 ft elev \\[meet @ Howarth Park's Boathouse\\] 4\\) Sat 
 8/22- Jack London State Historic Park\, May’s Clearing\, 3.5 mi
 les\, 820 ft elev \\[meet @ upper parking lot\, 2400 London Ran
 ch Road\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\\] 5\\) Sat 8/29 - Vista Trail 
 loop\, 3.5 miles\, 830 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 6\\) Sat
  9/5 – Stern \\+ Waterfall loop\, 2.7 miles\, 750 ft elev \\
 [meet @ main lot\\] 7\\) Sat 9/12 – Sonoma Valley Regional Par
 k & Lake Suttonfield loop\, 4.3\, miles\, 770 ft elev \\[meet a
 t Valley of the Moon Trailhead on Arnold Dr.\\] 8\\) Sat 9/19 
 – Hillside to Neptune picnic table\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elev 
 \\[meet @ white barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes or dates are
  subject to change depending on logistics. Wear appropriate footw
 ear for rocky/slippery trails and layers. Bring at least a quart
  \\(32oz\\) of water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will
  be limited to 35 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffsummer26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Tree Drawing in Mixed Media at Jack London State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T140000
UID:260627cwxhEzcBgEmpupFTL8IDBg
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nSaturday\, July 11\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 2:00 
 PM\n\nEvent Series\n\nView all classes in this series here.\n\nLocation\n\
 nJack London State Historical Park\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Wor
 kshops\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegist
 ration Cost:\n\n$75\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$5\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\
 n$80\n\nIn this one-day workshop\, participants will learn and practice fo
 undational drawing techniques while sketching the beautiful trees at Jack 
 London State Park. Each student will choose a tree to draw\, and then spen
 d time rendering their subject while receiving instruction in proportion a
 nd other key drawing skills.Once students have an established drawing\, th
 ey will explore the light and shadow on their tree with inventive colors i
 n watercolor. Practice and build your observational drawing skills\, spend
  time in nature\, and have fun with color!Discover the meditative benefits
  of a plein air art practice\, and gain a deeper appreciation for the natu
 ral world around you through close observation and intentional rendering. 
 No prior drawing experience necessary\; beginners welcome. All materials a
 re provided and all experience and skill levels are welcome!After the work
 shop you may choose to go hiking\, tour the museum\, or walk to the ruins 
 of the Wolf House.Important note: There is a Vehicle Entry Fee of $15. Aft
 er the kiosk\, veer to the right and proceed to the parking lot. All stude
 nts will meet the instructor in the parking lot and walk together to the w
 orkshop area. Dress for the weather and bring a water bottle and snacks or
  a bag lunch.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/plein-air-tree-drawing-july
 -2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
