BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mokuhanga (Ukiyo-e) Japanese Woodblock Printmaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T160000
UID:260728vCAfz8crCkmnWuLPwvAhbA
DESCRIPTION:Weekly every Sundays · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 9 –
  23\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 4:00 PM Short lunch break included\n\nLocation\
 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\
 nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$300\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$
 50\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$350\n\nIn this special three-part works
 hop\, participants will be introduced to the art of Japanese woodblock pri
 nting called Ukiyo-E technique. Tomoko Murakami\, an acclaimed Bay Area\, 
 Japanese-born printmaking artist\, will demonstrate the traditional Mokuha
 nga carving and printing process. Tomoko will introduce the relationship b
 etween positive and negative space in relief printing techniques\, includi
 ng Kento registration. Participants will learn to carve their own woodbloc
 ks using Japanese carving tools to create small multi-color woodblocks and
  create prints with non-toxic water-based inks on Japanese paper. Students
  will be able to develop an appreciation of Japanese woodblock prints\, ma
 terials\, processes and innovations. Learn to carve your own woodblocks an
 d create a small edition of multicolor prints! This class is perfect for b
 eginners as well as continuing students. All levels are welcome!Please not
 e: This class requires hand dexterity to maneuver the carving tools. Parti
 cipants should feel comfortable standing and using wood carving tools with
  sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/mokuhanga-japanese-woodbloc
 k-printmaking/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brazilian guitarist and composer Guinga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T200000
UID:2607282hQzUIHd-02RffhY0iQQ6w
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma Valley Jazz Society in partnership with the Sonoma 
 Petaluma Parks \\(SPPARKS\\) proud to present an intimate evening with int
 ernationally acclaimed Brazilian guitarist and composer Guinga\, performin
 g live at the historic Sonoma Mission San Francisco Solano on Sunday\, Aug
 ust 23\, 2026\, at 6:30 PM. Doors open at 6 PM.\n\nRecognized as one of Br
 azil’s most sophisticated and expressive musical voices\, Guinga has ear
 ned global admiration for his intricate harmonies\, lyrical depth\, and ge
 nre‑defying compositions that blend samba\, choro\, jazz\, and classical
  influences. His work has been recorded by legends including Elis Regina\,
  Michel Legrand\, Chico Buarque\, and Clara Nunes.\n\nThis rare West Coast
  appearance offers audiences a chance to experience Guinga’s artistry in
  one of Sonoma’s most iconic and intimate settings. The Mission’s warm
  acoustics and historic character provide a perfect backdrop for an evenin
 g of profound musical storytelling.\n\n“We are honored to bring an artis
 t of Guinga’s stature to Sonoma\,” said Jonathan Hsu of  the Sonoma V
 alley Jazz Society. “His music is deeply emotional\, technically brillia
 nt\, and unlike anything else in the world of contemporary guitar.”
LOCATION:Mission San Francisco Solano
URL:http://www.sonomavalleyjazzsociety.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chico Pinheiro Trio with Edu Ribeiro and Scott Thompson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T203000
UID:260721BEhHn6NsJ0qyiXkMV_ishg
DESCRIPTION:Chico Pinheiro is an exceptional guitarist with a beautiful so
 und and great fluidity\, a unique composer who blends Brazilian Music\, Cl
 assical Music\, and Jazz. Chico has released multiple albums to critical a
 cclaim\, and he has been nominated twice for the American Grammy Awards. J
 oin us for this special evening combining Brazilian brilliance and fine ar
 t at the Mahder Gallery. \n\nBorn and raised in São Paulo\, Brazil\, Chi
 co started playing the guitar when he was six. At 14\, he started work as 
 a studio session guitarist and soon began collaborating with a wide range 
 of artists in his hometown\, then in Brazil\, then abroad. Today\, Chico i
 s considered a leading figure in and outside the Brazilian music scene\, w
 ho has distinguished himself as a guitarist\, composer\, and arranger. Alo
 ng with his main projects\, he has collaborated with leading artists such 
 as Placido Domingo\, Dave Grusin\, Dianne Reeves\, Kurt Elling\, Danilo P
 érez\, Herbie Hancock\, Brian Blade\, Ron Carter\, Renee Rosnes\, Julian 
 Lage\, and esperanza spalding to name a few.  At this special concert\, h
 e will perform alongside Edu Rebeiro (drums) and Scott Thompson (bass). \
 n\nThe Healdsburg Jazz Collective will open for the Chico Pinheiro Trio wi
 th a unique program dedicated to Brazil. The Collective is headed by local
  favorite saxophonist Ruth Ahlers\, accompanied by Steve Weaver (trombone)
 \, Christian Foley-Beining (guitar)\, Chris Amberger (bass)\, and Mario Ap
 aricio (drums).
LOCATION:Paul Mahder Gallery
URL:https://healdsburgjazz.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
