BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bill Kirchen/Nina Gerber & Back pOrchEstra Peacetown concert Wed A
 ug 26 5p
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T200000
UID:260820lT5YDciyaECpcuGOd8I9_A
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra: American Roots music at Peacetown's Ives Park
  concert series opening for me ole band-mate Bill Kirchen (The Moonlighter
 s & Commander Cody) and his Austin TX Trio plus Nina Gerber\n\nWed\, Aug 2
 6 5:00-6:00\, Outdoors at 7400 Willow St\, Sebastopol\, CA 95472\n\nBill &
  Nina at 6:30-8:00 pm\n\nSee https://www.peacetown.org/summer-series-2026/
 2026/8/26/back-porchestra\n\n...and http://www.BackPorchEstra.com/shows.ht
 ml\n\nand https://www.billkirchen.com\n\nBack pOrchEstra is Tim Eschliman 
 (Etta James\, Commander Cody & His Western Airmen\, New Copasetics) on voc
 als & resonator guitar\, Bowen Brown (John Lee Hooker\, Tommy Castro\, Rhy
 thmtown-Jive) on drums\, Candy Girard (Delaney Bramlet\, Clint Black\, wit
 h Jerry Garcia on his album “Cats Down Under the Stars”) on violin\, J
 en Rund (Lumination) on bass\, Steve Black on guitar and special Guest Kat
 hy Kennedy on vocals.\n\nWe have a new single out!: https://orcd.co/7jjvmm
 x ... "What Does Your Heart Say?" - a Breez west coast rock\, a hopeful id
 ealistic Americana love song duet.\n\nPrevious Back pOrchEstra single: htt
 ps://orcd.co/lxz1l6v "I'm Wild About My Lovin'"\, ... celebrating the new 
 "Stories In The Heart" album\, hear it all now!: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n
 \n"The guitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin traces lines that oscil
 late between melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm section moves forward 
 with a tranquil groove that never rushes but never falters... Back pOrchEs
 tra delivers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human record. An album that 
 makes you want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\, and let the stories 
 do their work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine\n\n"*Stories In The Heart*\,
  retaining the charm inherent in this "retro" sound-music that feels more 
 relevant today than ever before-and serving as a testament to the richness
  of the musical community in San Francisco and the Bay Area. The album con
 firms his mastery of a wide array of genres\, effectively serving as a mus
 ical roadmap of American music... spanning blues\, Americana\, country\, r
 ock 'n' roll\, and rock-but even more so with their indie\, rockabilly\, T
 ex-Mex\, 1920s-style Cajun\, zydeco\, New Orleans\, Western swing\, and ne
 o-Motown sounds.... magnificent songs with a vintage\, retro flair\, featu
 ring excellent compositions characterized by fluid lines that never lose t
 heir rhythm and evoke vivid imagery. With this new album Back pOrchEstra a
 chieves-in perfect style-a homespun\, familiar ("downhome") sound that rec
 onciles us with the fine music of a bygone era." (translated from Italian)
  - Aldo Pedron\, Mescalina.it\n\nBack Porchestra's "Stories In the Heart":
  The opener\, 'Ever Think About It' is a Motown flavored Northern soul-sty
 led stomper\, though the violin solo is a little unexpected. The vocal is 
 just a little low in the mix too but maybe that just adds to the feel. No\
 , this hasn't come out of some obscure Detroit basement studio\; these guy
 s are from the San Francisco Bay Area! Perhaps less unexpected then is the
  imaginatively-rearranged version of Jim Jackson's 'I'm About My Lovin' br
 inging to mind Dan Hicks And His Hot Licks\, from the same area and who pl
 ayed a wide variety of rootsy music (mainly) from the '20s to the '40s. Ba
 ck Porchestra make things even more eclectic adding a couple or later deca
 des and a global base to the formula. Blg Al Anderson / Stephen Bruton's c
 omposition 'I Ain't Ever Slown Down'\, transformed into an appropriately d
 riving more or less straight Cajun number\, with Candy Girard's violin pla
 ying really rather wonderful (as it is throughout). - Norman Darwen\, BITS
  - Blues In The South\, March 2026\, Exmouth\, UK\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a 
 compact Shelter-in-Place-inspired musical combo ....going back to the basi
 cs... Formed for the first time the locked-down summer of 2020. The band d
 raws from new original material as well as reworked classics by Hank Willi
 ams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles
  ...even Christmas Jug Band tunes\n\n... check out the "Dusty Road I'm On"
  video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a 
 Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous 
 single\, the Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style "Ever Think About It\," is here: 
 https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-Music Cards available all o
 ver\, including https://www.globerecords.com\n\nmore at... https://www.Bac
 kpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTub
 e: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiN
 f\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestra.bsky.social\n\nRever
 b Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestra\n\nFacebook: https:/
 /www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/
 backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#americanrootsmusic\n\n#americanamusic\n\
 n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#backporchestra\n\n#acousticmusic\n\
 n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwriter\n\n#folkmusic\n\n#folkrock
LOCATION:Ives park
URL:https://www.peacetown.org/summer-series-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ask E. Jean Screening for Sonoma County NOW!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T203000
UID:260820eplx3a7r-0yFlnzBFzQaWQ
DESCRIPTION:National Women's Equality Day special showing! "Ask E. Jean\,"
  the thrilling story of E. Jean Carroll’s life\, from her early days as 
 Miss Cheerleader USA to her rise as a trailblazing journalist\, author\, a
 nd beloved advice columnist. Carroll broke barriers as the first female ed
 itor at Esquire\, Playboy\, and Outside\, helping to redefine women’s ro
 les in media with her sharp wit and fearless voice. In recent years\, she 
 reignited public discourse by standing up to power\, becoming the only wom
 an to beat Donald Trump twice in court \\(now under attack again\\)\, and 
 sparking a national conversation about truth\, accountability\, and resili
 ence. A portrait of an indomitable woman who proved it’s never too late 
 to reclaim your voice\, rewrite your story\, and change the world. This ev
 ent is a fundraiser for Sonoma County NOW. Come\, join us!
LOCATION:The Rialto Cinemas Sebastopol
URL:https://rialtocinemas.com/coming-soon/ask-e-jean-seb/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
