BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pregnant Worker Fairness Act and other ways to support employee wo
 rk-life balance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260827T123000
UID:260821hGnQ1eSg5EWU_OyPcKD1Wg
DESCRIPTION:Habrá servicio de interpretación al español Join us for thi
 s free educational seminar open to all Sonoma County employers\, business 
 leaders\, HR professionals\, and managers. The first session of this three
 -part series explores the Pregnant Worker Fairness Act and practical strat
 egies for supporting employees during pregnancy\, after childbirth\, and t
 hroughout the transition to parenthood. Presented by Samantha Pungprakeart
 i\, Associate\, Carle\, Mackie\, Power & Ross LLP\, the seminar combines e
 xpert employment legal reminders with discussion of innovative workplace p
 ractices that help employers attract\, retain\, and support talented emplo
 yees through work-life balance initiatives. Participants will learn: What 
 accommodations employers may be required to provide during pregnancy and a
 fter childbirth—and why those obligations are broader than many employer
 s realize. How to determine when an employee should remain in their positi
 on with reasonable accommodations versus when a leave of absence is approp
 riate. Unique ideas for providing flexibility and support to new and expec
 ting parents while strengthening employee engagement and retention. This s
 eminar is Part 1 of a free three-part series exploring how employers can b
 uild family-friendly workplaces while navigating employment law and suppor
 ting work-life balance for all employees. Upcoming sessions include: Part 
 2: Leave Protections & Supporting Employees with Growing Families – Unde
 rstand state and federal leave protections\, discuss strategies for suppor
 ting employees facing childcare challenges\, and explore how to create equ
 itable work-life balance policies that benefit employees with and without 
 children. Part 3: Family-Friendly Workplaces: Attracting & Retaining Talen
 t – Learn about lactation accommodation requirements\, employee benefits
  and compensation options\, and affordable\, high-impact workplace practic
 es that can help organizations recruit and retain top talent. The FREE ser
 ies is presented by the Santa Rosa Metro Chamber as part of its Workplace 
 & Workforce Innovation initiative\, helping employers build workplaces whe
 re employees and businesses thrive. This free series is made possible thro
 ugh funding from First 5 Sonoma County and Measure I.  Please RSVP
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Dowtown Square
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/896016423221801/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
