BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Flag Book Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T140000
UID:260808a9WvwRa8_Ui_5nFocJPf2Q
DESCRIPTION:Date & Time\n\nFridays\, August 21 – 28\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM 
 – 2:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 200\, Sam Morphy Community Room\n\nCategor
 y\n\nPrintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older
 \n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$125\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$20\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$145\n\nThis special book arts workshop is perfect for anyone
  interested in exploring a different twist on a creative book structure! J
 oin guest artist\, Bettina Pauly for a special introduction in how to crea
 te an original artistic concept flag book. Creation of this 3D book design
 \, will include a concertina fold\, glued 3” x 2” cardstock “flags
 ” into folds\, decoration of pages\, cover design\, assembly and book co
 ver finishing with bookbinding cloth.Originally invented by Hedi Kyle\, th
 e traditional flag book has small panels that cross each other when the bo
 ok opens and closes. The Flag Book is described as a portable\, expandable
  file that can display an array of materials in an animated way. It is mad
 e out of an accordion fold\, with small cards glued into the folds\, and a
  cover. Operating with the assistance of the accordion fold\, it has the f
 reedom to expand and retract. It can be read page by page or pulled apart 
 for the full effect of an uninterrupted scenario. Standing\, the Flag Book
  also will turn into a circular star book as the covers are held together 
 at the back. This workshop welcomes beginners\, and artists of all levels
 . The instructor will offer guided instruction in a supportive learning en
 vironment with a limited class size over the course of two sessions. The c
 lass materials fee will include paper and all the tools needed to create e
 ach of these projects. Students are welcome to bring their own paper sourc
 es or artwork they might choose to incorporate\, and are able to take home
  their very own book project at the end of the workshop. Please note: Thi
 s class requires some hand dexterity to maneuver bookbinding tools. Partic
 ipants should feel comfortable using tools with sharp edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-flag-book-m
 aking/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Japanese Fabric Beadmaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260828T160000
UID:260808NwLn8zumH0mRBoCetoppEg
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFridays Weekly · 2 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust
  28 – September 4\, 2026\n\n2:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 201\
 , Fiber Arts Studio\n\nCategory\n\nFiber Arts\n\nExperience Level\n\nBegin
 ning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$80\n\nMaterials Fee
 :\n\n$15\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$95\n\nLearn to create hand-rolled
  beads made from vintage Japanese recycled or remnant fabric. This is a tw
 o day workshop\, 2 hours each workshop. During the first class\, students 
 will choose from distinctive Japanese fabrics and learn the process of cut
 ting\, preparing the fabric and the rolling techniques to create handmade 
 beads. For the second workshop the participants will return with the fabri
 c beads they have completed at home and will learn how to design and assem
 ble a personal jewelry piece incorporating their fabric beads with a varie
 ty of provided glass and stone beads.Materials fee includes fabric\, adhes
 ive\, beads\, wire and findings.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/japanese-fabric-beadmaking/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
