 rance\, vocalizations\, and the evidence they leave behind. No experience 
 required. Must be age 18 years or older.
LOCATION:Fairfield Osborn Preserve
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/birds_of_osborn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi Gong at Barbieri Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T230000
UID:2608173jmPR9nDCU-tXyk1e9J-uA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an hour of movement. Qi Gong \\(pronounced "chee g
 ong"\\) is a gentle practice of movement\, breathing\, intention and mindf
 ulness. Think of it as meditation in motion. The movements are simple and 
 easy to learn. Everything can be adapted for a variety of abilities. All a
 re welcome...no experience necessary. You'll leave class feeling less stre
 ss and more of your inner vitality. Classes taughy by Marianne Benforado i
 s a licensed acupuncturist and certified Holden Qi Gong teacher. Students 
 describe her classes as welcoming and down to earth with good vibes sprink
 led on top. Drop in anytime it works for your schedule.
LOCATION:Barbieri Park
URL:https://feelbetteracu.com/events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Remember When: Family Make-In
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T150000
UID:260816QeW13YFQ_0eIymq0D5C95A
DESCRIPTION:Explore summer past and present through hands-on activities th
 at honor the sun\, water\, and collective joy. Create art with Edilia Mend
 ez of RAIZES Collective\, learn weaving techniques with textile artist Ale
 xander Hernandez\, and discover the magic of cyanotype photography with Br
 enna Hansen\, using sunlight to make beautiful blue prints. Throughout the
  afternoon\, enjoy opportunities to connect with artists\, family\, and fr
 iends in a welcoming atmosphere. Then\, get moving with a lively disco dan
 ce lesson before ending the day with a joyful live performance. Perfect fo
 r all ages\, this free community celebration invites everyone to make\, da
 nce\, and celebrate the season together. Saturday\, August 29\, 11 AM-3 PM
  Free Admission!
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1567106941512390/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
