BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of AntiNuclear Films and Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T210000
UID:2608153Is2BnYlp0OPbQ2l16UV1g
DESCRIPTION:Daniel Ellsberg's job at the Defense Dept. was "the design of 
 nuclear war plans." He came to consider it "the most evil planning that ha
 s ever existed in the history of humanity." As the world's powers begin a 
 new nuclear arms race\, join Veterans For Peace\, the Peace & Justice Cent
 er\, CodePink\, and the Green Party for a showing of two short films: one 
 based on interviews near the end of Daniel Ellsberg's life and another on 
 a resurrected sailboat that tried to sail to the Marshall Islands in the 1
 950's to stop nuclear testing. Discussion\, including with Ellsberg's wido
 w Patricia\, will follow the films and there will be music and light refre
 shments.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.pjcsoco.org/event---anti-nuke-films.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
