DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T120000
UID:260812UbwAgY8N1EeKs2VDopbB0Q
DESCRIPTION:Everyone is welcome to join us at The Kove\, a new community h
 ub for all ages of Marin County residents. Every Saturday morning\, meet a
 t The Kove to build connections and take part in programs that nourish hea
 lth\, learning and belonging\, including health & wellness talks\, connect
 ion to resources\, enrollment for our weekly food pantry\, and our Neighbo
 r Connection Hour at "Saturdays at The Kove"! The Kove is located in a wel
 coming space inside of Northgate Mall. Each Saturday features a different 
 physician or expert-led health and wellness talk with plenty of time to ge
 t your questions answered. Visit www.thekove.org to stay up-to-date!
LOCATION:The Kove community hub
URL:http://www.thekove.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yoga & Sound Healing with La Reina Marshall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
UID:260812Sv2JRldb6kCvr5nTGc-HKA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an outdoor yoga & sound healing session\n\nYoga be
 gins at 9am. This class is a vinyasa flow with the intention to provide an
  opportunity to slow down enough to feel deeply into your body\, to connec
 t mindfully with your breath\, and ultimately soothe your nervous system. 
 While strengthening and lengthening the body\, we will connect movement wi
 th breath\, and aim to strike a balance between effort and ease. We will c
 omplete this movement practice with a restorative reiki sound healing expe
 rience meant to soothe and nourish your physical and emotional body deeply
 . Accessible for all levels.\n\nFollowing class\, enjoy live music and com
 plimentary refreshments. Plus\, attendees are invited to stop by ME SPA at
  728 Farmers Lane to pick up product samples\, try a complimentary LED dem
 o\, and book an appointment on the spot for 10% off. Snap a photo at their
  spa selfie station and enter for a chance to win a 50-minute massage or f
 acial. L'Occitane will also be on-site guiding a DIY facial experience at 
 their wash station\, the perfect post-workout treat.\n\nMore about the ins
 tructor - La Reina Marshall:\n\nLa Reina Marshall RYT 500 has been practic
 ing yoga since 2005 and received her 200 hour certification at Soul Yoga i
 n June 2019. She is trained in trauma informed yoga\, yin yoga\, restorati
 ve yoga and sound healing. She completed trainings with Dolphin Method as 
 a certified Doula\, as well as Prenatal & Postnatal Vinyasa Yoga. La Reina
  is trained and attuned in Reiki I and II and Mastery levels. La Reina com
 pleted her 300 Hour yoga certifications with Soul Yoga in October of 2024.
  La Reina lives in beautiful Bennett Valley located in Santa Rosa\, Califo
 rnia. She currently teaches multiple public yoga classes at Soul Yoga. La 
 Reina is an Integrative Health Practitioner and loves helping people find 
 support in self healing while integrating a variety of modalities and has 
 worked in the healing arts for over 10 years.\n\nFor La Reina\, the practi
 ce of yoga\, sound healing and energy work are a path to emotional and phy
 sical wellness. She teaches a vinyasa inspired flow to create a grounded c
 ontainer to experience your body on the mat. The very act of being aware o
 f our bodies and feeling what we need to feel is how we live more fully. W
 ith compassion and authenticity\, you will have an opportunity to explore 
 your connection with the present moment using your breath as a guide. La R
 eina believes practicing vulnerability is the gateway for healing ourselve
 s\, and by doing so we contribute to the collective healing of those aroun
 d us.\n\nBy registering and attending this class\, you acknowledge that yo
 u have read and understand this Release and Waiver and accept and agree to
  the terms and provisions contained in this Release and Waiver.\n\nThis ou
 tdoor event will be held atThe Courtyard\, located between Salt & Straw (7
 00 Village Court) and Monti's (714 Village Court). Please wear layers\, su
 nscreen and don't forget your sunglasses!\n\nMats will be provided\, but y
 ou are welcome to bring your own mat for additional support. Please bring 
 your own water bottle.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village Courtyard
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/wellness-weekend-3/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
