DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 29 | 3:00 PM San Geronimo Valley Community C
 enter Courtyard\n\nAfter an epic day of health\, wellness\, laughter\, and
  wonderfully wacky competition at Valley Games X\, keep the celebration g
 oing with live music from New Monsoon in the Community Center courtyard 
 — and help us celebrate Helen Ferlino’s 50th birthday!\n\nOur hometow
 n heroes\, nationally touring band New Monsoon have deep roots in the Sa
 n Geronimo Valley and a devoted following. Known for their soulful blend o
 f rock\, groove\, improvisation\, and high-energy musicianship\, they’ve
  become beloved fixtures of the Bay Area music scene.\n\nCome wind down th
 e summer with friends\, neighbors\, families\, Valley Games competitors\, 
 and music lovers for an afternoon of great music and community.\n\nValley 
 Games by day. New Monsoon by afternoon. One big Valley celebration!
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://events.humanitix.com/valley-games-x
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Japanese Papermaking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T170000
UID:260808UUbakisXkEmIfTKVF97CZA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, August 29\, 2026 2:00 PM – 5:00 PM Su
 nday\, August 30\, 2026 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nEx
 perience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Bilingual\, Fiber Arts\,
  Printmaking\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n$180 – Registration Cost $
 25 – Materials Fee $205 – Total Registration Cost\n\nIn this workshop\
 , students will be introduced to the process of making Japanese paper. Jap
 anese paper\, often incorrectly referred to as rice paper\, is known for i
 ts great strength while appearing delicate and gossamer-thin. In this work
 shop\, students will learn the basics of preparing their own fiber\, hand 
 beating\, and forming sheets in the traditional nagashizuki method. Studen
 ts will take home wet sheets to dry at home with instructions.Please be aw
 are that papermaking is a wet activity –  wear clothing and shoes that 
 can get wet. Class involves some physical activity\, including standing an
 d arm movements. All supplies are provided through the materials fee. La m
 aestra habla español.Note: Please bring a bag lunch on Sunday.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/japanese-papermaking/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
