BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The TNG Reset - Why You Hurt Where You Do
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T111500
UID:260803soKeCMYF6UyyDGqnVPrmQQ
DESCRIPTION:If stretching provides only temporary relief—or sometimes ma
 kes you feel worse—the source of your discomfort may not be where you fe
 el the pain.\n\nThe TNG Reset is an interactive\, small-group workshop des
 igned to help you better understand your body’s compensation patterns an
 d recurring areas of tension.\n\nDuring the workshop\, you’ll explore:\n
 \nWhy stretching doesn’t always work\n\nThe difference between a shorten
 ed muscle and one that is overstretched and exhausted\n\nHow posture\, mov
 ement habits\, the glutes\, and the psoas can contribute to recurring tens
 ion\n\nTargeted ball-rolling and self-release techniques\n\nA realistic fi
 ve-minute reset routine you can use at home\n\nCome curious and wear comfo
 rtable clothing. You’ll leave with practical tools and a clearer underst
 anding of what may be contributing to your personal pain patterns.\n\nDate
 : Saturday\, August 29\, 2026 Time: 10:00–11:30 AM Location: Shimmery Al
 chemy Studio Address: 406 E Street\, Santa Rosa Price: $60 per person Led 
 by: Tiffany Gann of The Natural Gift Wellness Registration: Advance regist
 ration required\; limited to 10 participants.
LOCATION:Shimmery Alchemy
URL:http://www.tngmassage.com/events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T170000
UID:260803pmx0NIyjBEau1_GknkE3Rg
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
