DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T190000
UID:260803NEvksDFcLUKE4WZKCEH8oQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us Saturday\, August 29\, 2026 for our next Michael Leona
 rdi Foundation Music \\+ Awareness Concert hosted at The Barn Napa Valley/
 Car Club in downtown Napa from 4-7 pm\, featuring Dirty Cello\, 945 The Ba
 nd and Cherry Blonde! This event features and supports talented musicians 
 while raising awareness about staying safe from illicit fentanyl. In addit
 ion to music\, the afternoon will also feature guest speakers and resource
 s\, a silent auction\, and food and beverages for purchase.\n\nReserve you
 r spot with at $30 donation through Eventbrite or at the door: https://MLF
 MusicAwareness2026.eventbrite.com\n\nA special thank you to our event spon
 sors Tugboat\, Cana Ranch and to our community supporters Napa County\, Na
 pa Health and Human Services Agency\, and the Matthew Perry Foundation.\n\
 nWe're thankful to The Barn Napa Valley / Car Club for partnering with us 
 to bring our community together for an evening of music and awareness.\n\n
 To learn more about our organization\, visit michaelleonardifoundation.org
 .\n\nThe Michael Leonardi Foundation is funded in part by Napa County Heal
 th and Human Services Agency \\(HHSA\\) through Opioid Settlement Funds \\
 (OSF\\) to support prevention\, intervention\, treatment\, recovery\, and 
 other life-saving programs and services for individuals and families throu
 ghout the community.
LOCATION:Napa Valley Car Club
URL:https://MLFMusicAwareness2026.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T193000
UID:2608039y-BpUoORkqx2VKoqfaS1A
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare (after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s n
 ame). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to questi
 on it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the cash\,
  tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate–l
 ie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drops in
 to many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that res
 onates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six act
 ors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of Shake
 speare's other plays-in-progress (one of which becomes the famous Macbeth.
 )
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
