BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Safari West Presents! Our Conservation Liaison Kate Fox
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T203000
UID:260131AsW7aEyKaUO3erA_YiuVrw
DESCRIPTION:Conservation Dinner Series: Kate Fox joins us in the elephant 
 room after dinner to give a talk about her conservation work around Safari
  West\, especially the native species. The conservation dinner series is c
 omplimentary to all dinner guests. If you want to attend this presentation
 \, please call our reservations team at \\(707\\) 566-3667 or \\(800\\) 61
 6-2695 and they can book it for you. Dinner starts at 7:00 PM. About the S
 peaker:    Kate Fox is a graduate student at Sonoma State. She has had a s
 trong passion for all living things her entire life. A curiosity in verteb
 rates has driven her to assist in research efforts regarding California Ti
 ger Salamanders \\(Ambystoma californiense\\)\, California Red Legged Frog
 s \\(Rana draytonii\\)\, captive Southern White Rhinos \\(Ceratotherium si
 mum simum\\)\, and captive Giraffes \\(Giraffa camelopardalis\\). She is a
 lso the conservation liaison and an animal caretaker at Safari West. In he
 r conservation role\, she's been working towards making Safari West's wild
  space more compatible with the native wildlife. Bird boxes\, cover boards
 \, and more are all in place on property. She is excited to share the work
  that Safari West does for the native species and how you can get involved
 .
LOCATION:Safari West
URL:https://safariwest.com/calendar/safari-west-presents-our-conservation-
 liaison-kate-fox/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
