BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple U-Pick at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T113000
UID:2607313Hj8E3R130GiKwNWFw7_GQ
DESCRIPTION:**Our popular Apple U-Pick Experiences return for a second yea
 r!**\n\nExperience the magic of harvest season at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
 \, where you can hand-select the most flavorful Honeycrisp or Fuji apples 
 straight from our certified organic orchard.\n\nTimed entries from 8:30am.
  Last orchard entry at 11:30am.\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults\, $3 for child
 ren. Registration required.\n\nU-Pick apples: $4 per pound.\n\n**Apple U-P
 ick FAQs** \n\nDo I need a reservation? \n\nYes! Please reserve your tim
 e slot on our reservation site. Reservations help us ensure everyone has a
  wonderful experience without overcrowding.  \n\nCan I show up without a
  reservation? \n\nWe require reservations to maintain our capacity limit
 s and ensure everyone enjoys their visit to the fullest.  \n\nCan I canc
 el my reservation?  \n\nAbsolutely! You can cancel your reservation up 
 to 48 hours before your scheduled time by calling us at 707-823-3100. Plea
 se note that cancellations made less than 48 hours in advance will result 
 in forfeiture of the entrance fee. \n\nCan I bring my dog?  \n\nDogs a
 re not permitted in the orchard\, with the exception of service animals. T
 his policy helps ensure the safety and comfort of all our visitors. \n\nC
 an I bring a stroller into the orchard?  \n\nFor safety reasons\, strol
 lers aren't allowed in the orchard\, but you're welcome to leave yours at 
 the check-in area where it will be safe and waiting for you!  \n\nI requ
 ire mobility accommodations. Can I still pick apples in the orchard?  \n
 \nYes. Please call us on 707-823-3110 once you’re made a reservation and
  we can provide suitable transportation into our orchard.\n\nWhy is there 
 an entrance fee?  \n\nThe entrance fee helps us maintain our beautiful 
 orchard and keep our experienced staff on hand to ensure everyone has a sa
 fe and enjoyable experience. \n\nHow much are the apples?  \n\nOur del
 icious U-pick apples are $4.00 per pound.  \n\nWhat variety of apples wi
 ll we be harvesting?  \n\nYou'll be picking either Honeycrisp or Fuji a
 pples (depending on seasonal availability).  \n\nCan I harvest heirloom 
 apples?  \n\nWhile heirloom apples aren't available for U-pick\, we off
 er many wonderful heirloom varieties for purchase in our Farm Shop.  \n\
 nAre your apples organic?  \n\nYes\, all our apples are organically gro
 wn and certified annually by Oregon Tilth!
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/u-pick
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T143000
UID:260626b7LIZdO-OEqJmM8BbW5Rqg
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
 sanna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\
 n*Bliss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish*\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nH
 eirloom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\n*Smoked Bacon-Grain Must
 ard Dressing*\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian 
 Seven-Spiced Chicken Breast\n\n*Indonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable
  Ragout\, Balado Sauce*\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Van
 illa Burnt Basque Cheesecake\n\n*Raspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licori
 ce-Poached Cherries*\n\n*Brown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime*\n\n**Es
 tate Ingredients:**\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, L
 emons\, Olive Oil\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tom
 atoes\, Zucchini and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservat
 ions are required. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:With Regret: Comedy in the Deerfield Cave
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T203000
UID:260519jzIgxrFfU0uR7V-vR-BbPw
DESCRIPTION:Experience a one-of-a-kind night of entertainment as With Regr
 et Presents transforms the spectacular subterranean wine cave at Deerfield
  Ranch Winery into an intimate\, premium comedy club. This exclusive showc
 ase features a hand-picked lineup of the Bay Area’s top stand-up comedia
 ns performing live inside the winery's stunning cave tunnels. Guests can e
 njoy award-winning local wines and delicious dining options available insi
 de the cave before the laughter begins. Perfect for a unique date night or
  an unforgettable evening out in the valley. Doors open at 5:00 PM for win
 e and food\, and the comedy showcase kicks off promptly at 7:00 PM. Seatin
 g inside the cave is strictly limited. Advanced ticket purchase is highly 
 recommended.
LOCATION:Deerfield Ranch Winery
URL:https://luma.com/qmz0ndo5
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricoleur Vineyards Essentials Picnic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T153000
UID:260508KEfwUybdp02h0LeQCnwTHA
DESCRIPTION:Bricoleur Vineyards’ beloved Essentials Picnic pairs a b
 ottle of wine with charcuterie\, presented in a quintessential wicker bask
 et and a chic red wagon\, offering a relaxed and beautifully curated alfre
 sco wine country experience. Guests can enjoy their picnic in picturesque\
 , family- and dog-friendly settings across the estate—whether on the Pav
 ilion lawn\, beneath the trellis by the pond\, or at the picnic tables nes
 tled within the culinary and rose gardens. With exceptional wines\, thou
 ghtfully crafted foods\, and sweeping vistas\, a visit to Bricoleur Vin
 eyards offers a laid-back\, family-friendly atmosphere featuring lawn ga
 mes\, board games\, scavenger hunts\, and catch-and-release fishing.
LOCATION:Bricoleur Vineyard
URL:https://bricoleurvineyards.com/pages/visit?srsltid=AfmBOoq4MRc2MHal1tH
 0HwUmLbCHlVrPlsnizqNwrRFitw3UKui4rRJV
