 ble afternoon of live music\, great food\, family fun\, community resource
 s\, prevention\, remembrance and hope.**\n\nEnjoy live performances by **W
 onder Bread 5 and The Illeagles**\, 8+ food vendors\, beer & wine\, kids a
 ctivities\, animals\, community and health resources\, speakers\, free Nar
 can and fentanyl test strips\, and more.\n\nThis year's event will also fe
 ature an extraordinary memorial installation with approximately **350 over
 sized portraits from the Today I Matter Poster Project** displayed across 
 the hillside—the project's first large-scale memorial display of its kin
 d on the West Coast—along with **more than 100 memorial crosses** honori
 ng lives lost to substance use and overdose.\n\n**Presented by Sax's Joint
  and benefiting Micah's Hugs.**\n\nCome for the music\, food and fun—and
  leave with information that could save a life.\n\n**Sunday\, August 30 | 
 3–8 PM** **Pronzini Farms | Petaluma** **Kids 12 & under FREE**
LOCATION:Pronzini Farms
