DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T220000
UID:260820enz38oRce0uckzLNdNE7uA
DESCRIPTION:Raised in the Bay Area\, DJ Cal has gained a reputation for do
 ing multi-genre set lists designed to move the crowds with a blend of Trap
 \, EDM\,Hip-Hop and Reggaeton music. He calls the city of Santa Rosa his h
 ome\, but you might’ve heard his mixes on-air across the nation \\(San F
 rancisco\, Las Vegas\, Orlando\, Palms Springs\, etc.\\). He currently hol
 ds a spot as a Mixshow DJ on Fresno California B95\, with Teezzy Radio\, L
 ast Call and Friday night street party. DJ CAL has several Bay Area and No
 rthern California venues under his belt and you can catch him performing a
 nd hanging out with the hottest names in music around the Bay. He also has
  created his own day party\, "Brunch Behavior" that has gained much popula
 rity in the North Bay. Also\, his work has been supported and featured by 
 various blogs\, websites and record pools\; DJ City\, MyMP3Pool\, BpmSupre
 me and SmashTheClub\, and more. DJ CAL has worked hard to make his own mar
 k in the music industry.
LOCATION:Eight Ball
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108787234?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine & Wild - Sheep
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T193000
UID:260820XcIQ8c7DmUKNBpDY-VQiDQ
DESCRIPTION:Join the Parks Foundation for an engaging presentation\, the t
 hird installment of our 2026 Wine & Wild education series—where nature\,
  community\, and great wine come together. We will be joined by guest pres
 enter Cori Carlson of Nature Protein Pasture to discuss the important role
  sheep grazing plays in managing American Canyon’s open space.\n\nWe wil
 l explore the surprising connections between grazing animals\, healthy soi
 ls\, thriving wildlife\, and clean waterways. Through stories\, photos\, a
 nd examples from right here in American Canyon\, you’ll discover how car
 efully managed grazing benefits native grasslands\, supports birds and pol
 linators\, improves watershed health\, and helps create more resilient eco
 systems. From the microscopic organisms living beneath our feet to the haw
 ks soaring overhead\, every part of our local environment is connected. Le
 arn how healthy soils store water\, support native plants\, improve habita
 t for wildlife\, and contribute to the health of the Napa River watershed.
  You’ll also learn why grazing has long been a natural part of Californi
 a’s grassland ecosystems and how today’s land managers use sheep as on
 e of several tools to care for parks\, open spaces\, and natural areas.\n\
 nArrive early for the wine social and special wool art craft activity\, wh
 ich begin at 5:30 pm. The evening includes two special guests: Napa Valley
  Vintners and the American Canyon Soroptimists. The Napa Valley Vintners w
 ill be on-site to pour a selection of Napa Valley wines. The American Cany
 on Soroptimists will lead a small craft project during the wine reception.
  Wine & Wild is a free\, wildlife education series presented by the Americ
 an Canyon Community & Parks Foundation. The quarterly series features doce
 nt-led presentations hosted by local partner wineries. Wildlife presentati
 ons are approximately one-hour and may include meet-and-greets with ambass
 ador animals when appropriate. The wildlife presentation is free and open 
 to the public
LOCATION:Wetlands Edge Trail
URL:https://www.acparks.org/events/wine-wild-821-596-989-376/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
