DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the flavors of the Mediterranean with this relaxed s
 ummer lunch menu. Learn how to make the most of your backyard or farmer's 
 market bounty with this demonstration class taught by local cookbook autho
 r Stephanie Klassen.\n\nShe'll show you how to turn those overflowing bask
 ets of summer veggies into a cool Summer Garden Gazpacho\, a colorful Prov
 encal Vegetable Galette and Green Bean-Feta Salad. \\(And don't forget Non
 na's Olive Oil Cookies for dessert!\\) After the demo\, we'll sit down tog
 ether for an al fresco lunch overlooking our beautiful organic orchards.\n
 \nWhat to Expect:\n\n\\*A hands-on cooking demonstration in our charming A
 pple Cottage kitchen\n\n\\*Expert tips from Stephanie on creating deliciou
 s dishes using fresh\, local produce\n\n\\*A sit-down lunch featuring the 
 dishes you just watched being made\, enjoyed at a table overlooking our ap
 ple orchard\n\n\\*A signature refreshment: citrus shrub\, freshly pressed 
 apple cider or apple cider spritz\\*\n\nA scenic ride in our apple-themed 
 trolley from the Farm Shop to the Apple Cottage\n\n\\*10% off all Farm Sho
 p purchases on the day of the class\n\nStephanie Klassen is the author of 
 seven cookbooks\, including A Little Taste of San Francisco and Honey from
  Flower to Table. She has taught seasonal cooking at farmers markets and o
 ther venues from Brooklyn to Berkeley\, including the Ferry Plaza Farmers'
  Market in San Francisco and the Gravenstein Apple Fair in Sebastopol. She
  has cooked at numerous artists' and writers' retreats including the Headl
 ands Center for the Arts in Sausalito\, and studied organic farming at the
  Center for Agrocology at UC Santa Cruz.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/618724/harv
 est-cooking-learn-and-lunch-with-stephanie-klassen
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
