BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Linocut Stamp Carving Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T133000
UID:260817_I7xydwqZ0O_3QxnsHFMCQ
DESCRIPTION:Discover the creative art of linocut printmaking with Bay Area
  artist Ana Bianchi in this hands-on workshop designed for beginners and c
 urious makers alike.\n\nYou’ll learn the fundamentals of stamp carving a
 nd relief printing while exploring pattern\, imagery\, and repeatable desi
 gn through playful experimentation. Beginning with an easy-to-carve white 
 eraser before progressing to professional rubber carving blocks\, particip
 ants will gain confidence using carving tools\, safely handling materials\
 , and understanding the unique reverse-image process of printmaking.\n\nSa
 turday\, September 5\, 10:30 a.m. – 1:30 p.m.\n\n$78 for members\, $95 f
 or non-members | Includes Garden admission. Please check in at the Center 
 for Learning & Engagement. To learn more and sign up\, click “Register
 ” and explore the “Info” tab on the registration page.\n\n**Please n
 ote that a $10 materials fee is required for this workshop and is not in
 cluded in the registration price.** Participants should bring $10 cash\, p
 ayable directly to the artist on the day of the workshop. Material kits wi
 ll be available upon arrival and include all of the tools and supplies n
 eeded for the class\, so no additional materials are required.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/linocut-stamp-carving-workshop-1030-am-130-pm
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Intermediate 4-Week Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T140000
UID:260817KgN9G9dB4ke424EPS5Mxkw
DESCRIPTION:Take your dancing to the next level in this focused\, high-ene
 rgy intensive! Designed for dancers who already know the fundamentals. Cub
 an salsa Intermediate class will move beyond basic steps to focus on compl
 ex partner work patterns\, advanced body styling\, dynamic musicality\, an
 d the authentic flow of Cuban Casino.\n\n• 4-week course\, Saturdays\n\n
 • Date: September 5 – September 26 \\(4-week\\)\n\n• Time: 1:00 pm 
 – 2:00 Pm\n\n• Location: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8\, San Rafael\, CA\
 n\nRegistration Note: This class requires a minimum of 8 registrations to 
 run. Please register early so we can secure the session! Please no walk-in
 s\n\nPrerequisites\n\n• To ensure a fluid\, fast-paced learning environm
 ent\, this is an Intermediate level\n\nRequirement: You must have comple
 ted a Beginner Cuban Salsa course or have a solid grasp of beginner fundam
 entals \\(including basic footwork\, timing\, standard left/right turns\, 
 and fundamental partner connection\\).\n\nWhat We Will Cover\n\n• Advanc
 ed Partnerwork: Intricate Cuban Casino patterns\, seamless transitions\, 
 and directional changes.\n\n• Styling & Body Movement: Incorporating au
 thentic Cuban body isolation and natural expression into your dancing.\n\n
 • Musicality & Connection: Refining lead/follow mechanics to hit musica
 l breaks and accents naturally.\n\n• Intensive Structure: We will kick 
 off with a quick body isolation warm-up and advanced footwork exercises be
 fore diving straight into partnerwork technique and practical\, social-rea
 dy combinations.\n\nCome dance with us\, elevate your technique\, and expe
 rience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive and welcoming environ
 ment!\n\nImportant Details\n\n• Arrival: Please arrive 10 minutes befor
 e class starts \\(2:50 PM\\) to check in.\n\n• Shoe Policy: No floor-ma
 rking shoe soles allowed on the dance floor. 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8\, S
 an Rafael\, CA\n\n• September 5 – September 26 \\(4-week\\)\n\n• 1:0
 0 pm. – 2:00 pm
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa-intermediate/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
