BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Garden Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T140000
UID:260605pjDr2U0n_kGj_rNz_IdHxw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided tour of the Occidental Arts & Ecology Cen
 ter's demonstration gardens and living landscapes. Led by rotating OAEC st
 aff\, these tours offer an opportunity to explore our diverse food\, medic
 inal\, pollinator\, and native plant gardens while learning about the ecol
 ogical principles that guide our work. \n\nWhen: Tours start at 1 pm ever
 y first and third Saturday of the month\, April through October. \n\nWher
 e: Tours start and end at the OAEC Nursery. 15290 Coleman Valley Rd\, Occi
 dental\, CA 95465. Upper Driveway. \n\nImportant Information:\n\nNo regis
 tration required—just show up!\n\nPlease use the second driveway and par
 k in the upper lot near the greenhouses.\n\nThe tour route includes steep 
 hills and unpaved dirt and gravel paths. Sturdy shoes\, a brimmed hat\, an
 d weather-appropriate layers are recommended.\n\nIf you require mobility s
 upport or have other accessibility needs\, please call ahead so we can acc
 ommodate you. Monday–Friday\, contact the main office at \\(707\\) 874-1
 557 ext. 101.\n\nA highlight of every tour is the OAEC Nursery\, a nonprof
 it nursery dedicated to uplifting ecologically and culturally important pl
 ants. The nursery features a wide selection of perennial food crops\, medi
 cinal and native plants\, and an ever-evolving collection of annual vegeta
 bles and herbs adapted to our region.
LOCATION:Occidental Arts and Ecology Center
URL:https://oaec.org/events/tours/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Star Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T230000
UID:260514izpKNSKZ3Uq9WvfNpgeaEw
DESCRIPTION:Public Star Parties are the heart of the Robert Ferguson Obser
 vatory—your monthly invitation to experience the wonder of the night sky
  like never before. Whether you’re a lifelong astronomy enthusiast or si
 mply curious about what lies beyond our planet\, these gatherings offer so
 mething magical for everyone.Each month includes a variety of engaging ast
 ronomy presentations led by our expert docents. You’ll hear fascinating 
 stories about the cosmos and the science behind some of the objects you’
 ll soon be observing. These talks set the stage for an unforgettable night
  under the stars.Step outside into the darkness of Sugarloaf Ridge State P
 ark\, where the skies open up in breathtaking clarity. You’ll have the c
 hance to explore the universe through three of RFO’s massive telescopes\
 , each powerful enough to reveal extraordinary detail: lunar craters\, pla
 nets\, star clusters\, glowing nebulae\, distant galaxies\, and more. In a
 ddition\, a field of smaller telescopes brought and operated by dedicated 
 volunteers\, creates a dynamic\, community-powered observing experience.Ev
 ery month offers a new selection of celestial treasures\, and our friendly
 \, knowledgeable docents are excited to guide you. They’ll help you navi
 gate the night sky\, answer questions\, and point out objects that many pe
 ople never get the chance to see.Come experience the excitement\, curiosit
 y\, and shared sense of discovery that make Public Star Parties such a che
 rished RFO tradition. Free for members—and unforgettable for everyone!
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/public-star-parties-2026-tickets-240100
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T120000
UID:260514Zixe0B4erEKBv0GjNEKA_Q
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bricoleur Vineyards Essentials Picnic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T153000
UID:26050819dA1B3fbkebCm8rr0q9jg
DESCRIPTION:Bricoleur Vineyards’ beloved Essentials Picnic pairs a b
 ottle of wine with charcuterie\, presented in a quintessential wicker bask
 et and a chic red wagon\, offering a relaxed and beautifully curated alfre
 sco wine country experience. Guests can enjoy their picnic in picturesque\
 , family- and dog-friendly settings across the estate—whether on the Pav
 ilion lawn\, beneath the trellis by the pond\, or at the picnic tables nes
 tled within the culinary and rose gardens. With exceptional wines\, thou
 ghtfully crafted foods\, and sweeping vistas\, a visit to Bricoleur Vin
 eyards offers a laid-back\, family-friendly atmosphere featuring lawn ga
 mes\, board games\, scavenger hunts\, and catch-and-release fishing.
LOCATION:Bricoleur Vineyard
URL:https://bricoleurvineyards.com/pages/visit?srsltid=AfmBOoq4MRc2MHal1tH
 0HwUmLbCHlVrPlsnizqNwrRFitw3UKui4rRJV
