BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tomales Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:2608058Pnm0bkNB0ijUuAdV8fBnQ
DESCRIPTION:The **Tomales Festival** will be held at High Noon on Labor Da
 y Sunday\, September 6th. Join us in the Community Park (in between the Ca
 tholic church and the William Tell House) to celebrate with friends and ne
 ighbors. This year we're featuring music by the Blues Defenders\, plus fre
 sh oysters\, beer\, wine\, food\, and drink. Local arts and crafts\, plus 
 displays from local organizations and non-profits.\n\nThe festival is (and
  always has been) created\, organized\, and carried out by volunteers from
  the local community. This local tradition has quite a history: it was the
  Swiss-Italian celebration from 1888 until 1994\, when it became Founder's
  Day and later the Tomales Festival. That's 138 years worth of parades\, p
 icnics\, and parties. This event benefits the Tomales Town Hall\, which is
  a 501(c)3 non-profit community center.\n\nSpecial thanks to **Kathryn LeM
 ieux** for once again allowing us to use her whimsical cow painting as our
  festive logo. And thanks to our contributors. The **Hog Island Oyster Com
 pany** and **The Marshall Store** contributed the shellfish. **Morris Dist
 ributing** is providing our beer supply. **Recology Sonoma/Marin** is prov
 iding trash containers and is donating garbage service. We are grateful to
  our sponsor **Marin Agricultural Land Trust (MALT)**.\n\nSign ups for vo
 lunteers\, exhibitors\, vendors\, and more right are currently available. 
 Write to festival@TomalesTownHall.org or see the website: https://www.toma
 lestownhall.org/tomalesfest. Booth reservations end **August 15th**.
LOCATION:Tomales Community Park
URL:https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London and Japan: Connections Across the Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T110000
UID:260803mxmSsANbF0ivukM0Mcjeyw
DESCRIPTION:As part of a series co-hosted by Jack London Park Partners and
  the Jack London Society\, this is a rare opportunity to hear distinguishe
 d scholars from Japan present their research exploring the lives and relat
 ionships that connected Jack London with Japanese immigrants in early twen
 tieth-century California.\n\n**Professor Takaharu Mori** will explore Jack
  London’s relationships with Japanese immigrants\, focusing on Yoshimats
 u Nakata and Kanae Nagasawa\, a descendant of samurai and one of Californi
 a’s most influential early winemakers at Fountain Grove Winery in Santa 
 Rosa. Through their stories\, the presentation reveals the personal and cu
 ltural connections that linked Jack London with members of the Japanese co
 mmunity in Northern California.\n\n**Nagako Muto\, Ph.D.\,** a scholar of 
 classical Japanese literature\, will examine the remarkable 1914 diary of 
 Yoshimatsu Nakata\, a Japanese immigrant who lived and worked closely with
  Jack London. Nakata’s firsthand observations provide an intimate view o
 f London’s daily life\, physical challenges\, and interactions with Cali
 fornia’s legal and cultural landscape.\n\nProfessor Mori’s former stud
 ent\, **Dr. Kaoru Nishihara**\, will conclude the program with a brief pre
 sentation highlighting her own research into Jack London’s changing view
 s of Japan and the Japanese people.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-speaker-series-part-4/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:2608038HTkb4OhNEGqQC7vUG0fvQ
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T140000
UID:2608032wP6itAhEkO6fytYbqjZ8Q
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare (after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s n
 ame). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to questi
 on it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the cash\,
  tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate–l
 ie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drops in
 to many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that res
 onates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six act
 ors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of Shake
 speare's other plays-in-progress (one of which becomes the famous Macbeth.
 )
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mountain Regional Park\, Pythian 
 Rd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T110000
UID:260726ZBlK8SXqtkeRJ28j6BIumw
DESCRIPTION:Shuttle also offered on Sunday\, September 6.\n\nHow it
  works: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will leave from either Su
 garloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center \\(making a brief stop
  at the Goodspeed parking lot\\) or Hood Mountain Regional Park
 ’s Pythian Rd parking lot \\(with a brief stop at the equestr
 ian lot\\). Make a reservation to ride to the other end of the
  trail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride back. We recomme
 nd riding first and hiking back to your car afterward– no wor
 ries about how long you take to finish your adventure. The hike
  should take 3½ to 4½ hours depending on your pace\; the dis
 tance is about 7.4 miles one-way with approximately 2\,300ft of 
 elevation gain. \n\nBring at least 64 oz of water\, sun protecti
 on \\(the majority of the trail is exposed\\)\, a good paper ma
 p \\(some of the trail signs on Hood Mtn Regional Park are sti
 ll damaged from the 2020 wildfire and trails might not be well
  marked\\)\, and if desired\, hiking poles\, a friend\, and a l
 unch.\n\nIf you are riding from Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fil
 ls up quickly. If it is full\, please park at the main lot an
 d pick up the shuttle at the Visitor Center \\(you will have t
 o hike a mile back to the main lot from the bottom of the ca
 nyon/Goodspeed lot\\). If the Hood Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, ple
 ase park at the Equestrian Lot\, by the Hood House\, in Los Gu
 ilicos.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026sepsatshuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
