BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T000000
UID:260312gOeZL22j0U2zKxoaXi9_tg
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lucinda Williams\, Rod
 ney Crowell\, Steve Earle\, Neil Finn\, Patty Griffin\, Chuck Prophet\, an
 d Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a deep groove. \
 n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he developed a unique con
 nection to music early on. His father worked as a trash collector\, and he
  would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 records. Each find
  felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were covered in d
 irt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of discovering new 
 sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop the needle and 
 immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimage to Texas with
  just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal was to dive int
 o the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters. Austin\, know
 n as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countless opportuniti
 es for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters' nights became 
 his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, listening to other
 s share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he resides in Sonoma 
 County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and singer-songwrit
 er for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invites everyone to j
 oin him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one person at a time i
 n this vast and unpredictable world we live in.\n\nA.M. Sessions \n\nCheck
  out the latest album from S.R. Laws-  "A.M. Sessions." It's a collection 
 of songs that I am incredibly proud of\, crafted with the help of old frie
 nds and intrepid new collaborators. I can tell you more about it sometime.
  Come out and grab a copy at one of the shows or you can find it online. 
 “\n\n“ It is through forthright lyrics that are personal and earnest\,
  that he \\(Laws\\) composes lyrical pictures. Taking snapshots from the m
 ost common walks of life filtered through his own joy and tribulations.”
   - David Sampson - Producer Studio Secti West\n\n“..relaxed mid-tempo A
 mericana\, capturing in each song the rhythmic pocket Laws is known for cr
 eating.” -  Coyote Music Review 2024\n\n“...His lyrics simply tell fir
 st-person stories from his own life. Nothing fancy\, he's not writing to i
 mpress--he pours himself\, as is\, into each phrase and melody.”- Rebecc
 a Roudman- Dirty Cello Radio Hour KRCB Radio 104.9 FM\n\n“A.M. Sessions 
 is worth your while.” - Wiley Koepp- Texas Drummer
LOCATION:Napa Palisades Saloon
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107907391?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T160000
UID:260312Crw4NDRN60au2D61FR3ZAg
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Tasting Salon (Indoors Only)
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-brandlin-estate-win
 e-food-tasting-experience/18318441/2026-09-08T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Bath with Laura Benson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260908T203000
UID:260710vTaLALH5aEqg9RVp0JRNBw
DESCRIPTION:Rest & Renew at our Sound Bath! Support your nervous system\, 
 release anxiety and stress\, and harmonize your body\, mind and spirit on 
 the 2nd Tuesday of every month! Laura Benson has a Masters in Intuition Me
 dicine\\(R\\) and is a certified sound healer who will guide you through a
  gentle meditation before each sound bath session. Bring your own yoga mat
  & blanket and come ready to rest and renew! In the OCA Studio. Sliding sc
 ale pricing $25-$35.  Register A sound bath is a whole-body\, immersive li
 stening experience. During a sound bath\, participants often sit or lie do
 wn\, and are surrounded by the mostly non-melodic soundscapes created by a
  range of instruments played by the sound bath facilitator. Hence\, they a
 re "bathed" in sound. Sound therapy is a non-invasive healing modality tha
 t utilizes the physical and physiological interactions of sound on our bod
 ies and nervous systems to produce therapeutic results. In a sound healing
  session\, specific sonic frequencies are used to soothe the central nervo
 us system\, calm the breath\, and quiet the mind by encouraging the brain 
 to move into more relaxed states\, down from beta \\(fight-or-flight\\) an
 d into theta and alpha waves. This increases present-moment awareness and 
 reduces stress and anxiety. Sound baths have been found to be effective in
  improving mood\, cognitive function\, and overall mental\, physical\, and
  spiritual wellbeing. Crystal bowl sound baths are particularly powerful i
 n that each bowl is tuned to a specific frequency that corresponds with a 
 different chakra\, or energy center\, of the body. Based on specific needs
 \, a practitioner can focus on releasing tension or clearing out stuck ene
 rgy in specific chakras by playing certain bowls or intervals. While atten
 ding a sound bath\, you may experience physical sensations brought out by 
 the crystal sound bowls or gong\, such as tingling in your limbs or scalp\
 , slowing of your breathing\, eye flutters\, or small muscle spasms. Not t
 o worry! These sensations often indicate the release of tension or emotion
 al energy stored in the body's energy systems.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/rest-renew-
 monthly-sound-bath-l5n5c-wchlw-38gmc-rw262-hd6w3-nlnhm-bn8b8-d74pg-d79je-w
 x3an-ampe7-zckp7-gndtj-32c6f-4y8an-wsmxr-y3rtb-8k62p-lx4gx-36kl7-5kgyd
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
