BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:San Fran Halen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T220000
UID:260819sPxCxF0RikOxUPsW9BUomA
DESCRIPTION:Van Halen took all the best elements of 60s and 70s rock\, fus
 ed them with the panache and pageantry of vaudeville\, shot them into orbi
 t with high velocity guitar unlike the world had ever seen. From Runnin' w
 ith the Devil to Jump\, they single-handedly saved hard rock and ushered i
 n the glorious musical excesses of the 80s. San Fran Halen is a group of S
 an Francisco Bay Area pros who have joined the ranks of the world's best V
 an Halen tributes to pay homage to the joy etched in the indelible grooves
  on the sacred platters we have cherished since childhood. Ryan Cominskey 
 on drums\, Michael Freeman on bass\, Rob Spinosa on guitar\, and rock n ro
 ll ringmaster Mikki J. Fox have sworn on their honor to do their best to d
 o their duty to bring the party to you like it's 1984. It's never too late
  to have a happy adolescence. Opening Act Illegitimate AC/DC is the North 
 bay's ultimate tribute to the greatest rock band ever\, AC/DC. The band hi
 ghlights the Bon Scott era but steps into Brian Johnson territory as well.
  Fronted by Will Cotter and backed by 4 seasoned veterans of rock\, this a
 ct will make it seem like you've just seen the real deal\, 30 years ago. T
 he band is committed to keeping the music true to form\, with no tricks or
  fancy effects\, just pure\, straight-up Rock and Roll. BUY IN ADVANCE! TI
 CKETS AT THE DOOR ZONE C ONLY. Showtime 7:30pm\, doors open 6:30pm
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/san-fran-halen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
