BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Beginner Hiking for Fitness
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T130000
UID:260701GoNpgbFG7kiZMHlmSVL0HQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this fitness program\, where the leaders w
 ill guide you on a series of 8 weekly hikes with the challenge
  increasing each week. Before the first hike\, the leader will 
 discuss proper shoes\, hydration\, incorporating hiking poles\, pro
 per pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for the long rout
 e up Brushy Peaks Trail\, where hikers can enjoy the beautiful 
 vistas.\n\nThe following is a list of possible routes selected fo
 r this hiking series: 1\\) Sat 8/1 - White Barn to Uranus\, 2.1
  miles\, 180 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 2\\) Sat 8/8 - Me
 adow- Hillside loop\, 3 miles\, 490 ft elev \\[meet @ white bar
 n\\] 3\\) Sat 8/15 - Lake Ralphine & Spring Lake loop\, 4.3 mil
 es\, 420 ft elev \\[meet @ Howarth Park's Boathouse\\] 4\\) Sat 
 8/22- Jack London State Historic Park\, May’s Clearing\, 3.5 mi
 les\, 820 ft elev \\[meet @ upper parking lot\, 2400 London Ran
 ch Road\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\\] 5\\) Sat 8/29 - Vista Trail 
 loop\, 3.5 miles\, 830 ft elev \\[meet @ white barn\\] 6\\) Sat
  9/5 – Stern \\+ Waterfall loop\, 2.7 miles\, 750 ft elev \\
 [meet @ main lot\\] 7\\) Sat 9/12 – Sonoma Valley Regional Par
 k & Lake Suttonfield loop\, 4.3\, miles\, 770 ft elev \\[meet a
 t Valley of the Moon Trailhead on Arnold Dr.\\] 8\\) Sat 9/19 
 – Hillside to Neptune picnic table\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elev 
 \\[meet @ white barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes or dates are
  subject to change depending on logistics. Wear appropriate footw
 ear for rocky/slippery trails and layers. Bring at least a quart
  \\(32oz\\) of water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will
  be limited to 35 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/beghffsummer26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sturgeon’s Mill Open Demonstration Run
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T150000
UID:260610f60usimwA0yTdY68RZhR5A
DESCRIPTION:Step into a true piece of California history at Sturgeon’s M
 ill\, a fully operational **steam-powered sawmill founded in 1914**. Unlik
 e a replica\, this is an authentic working museum where the **original mac
 hinery still runs today**\, offering a rare chance to see early 20th-centu
 ry industry in action.\n\n**Dates:** June 20-21 | August 1-2 | September 1
 2-13\n\n**Time:** 10:00 AM - 3:00 PM (crew breaks for lunch 12:00 PM -1:00
  PM)\n\n**Location:** 2150 Green Hill Rd\, Sebastopol\, CA\n\nWatch live s
 team demonstrations as the mill comes to life\, explore historic equipment
 \, and learn how local lumber mills helped build Sonoma County and the gre
 ater Bay Area. Docent-led tours run throughout the day\, or you can explor
 e at your own pace.\n\nCome experience the sights\, sounds\, and stories o
 f a working mill where history still runs on steam.\n\n**Highlights:**\n\n
 Live operation of a historic steam-powered sawmill\n\nAll-original equipme
 nt from over 100 years ago\n\nGuided tours and hands-on exploration\n\nBla
 cksmith shop\, gardens\, and farm animals\n\nFood available for purchase f
 rom the cook shack\n\nBring a picnic and enjoy the beautiful redwood setti
 ng\n\n**Good to Know:**\n\nAdmission is **free - no tickets required**\n\n
 Donations are appreciated to support preservation\n\nFree parking availabl
 e on site.
LOCATION:Sturgeon's Mill
URL:http://www.sturgeonsmill.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
