SUMMARY:Hook and Ladder Vineyards and Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T123000
UID:251219jEE5kuyMCU69FWnA0ZVFAw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Vineyards & Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107647243?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heels Class with Masha (4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T203000
UID:2608084-UC-cARp0ep6jbA77aq_A
DESCRIPTION:September 14 – October 5\n\nHeels Class — Open to All Leve
 ls\n\nStep into your confidence and learn the foundations of dancing in he
 els in a supportive\, no-pressure environment. This class is designed for 
 beginners and anyone looking to build strength\, balance\, and style from 
 the ground up.\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\nThe Fundamentals: Learn how to balanc
 e\, walk\, and groove safely and confidently.\n\nEmpowering Choreography: 
 Dive into a fun\, expressive routine that celebrates your unique style.\n\
 nA Supportive Community: Dance alongside a non-judgmental group focused on
  self-expression\n\nWe’ll focus on this heels class:\n\n– Walking with
  confidence and control – Basic technique\, posture\, and lines – Musi
 cality and rhythm – Simple choreography to help you feel expressive and 
 empowered\n\nExpect a fun\, encouraging space where you can explore your f
 emininity\, build body awareness\, and grow at your own pace. No experienc
 e needed—just bring your energy and a pair of heels you feel comfortable
  in \\(or start in socks!\\).\n\nAll levels welcome. Come as you are\n\n4-
 weeks \, September 14 – October 5\n\nWE NEED AT LEAST 5 people for this 
 class\, please sign up early – no walk ins.\n\nMonday 7:30 PM – 8:30 P
 M
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/heels-with-masha/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
